    text: 'Most `/api/v1` endpoints have no rate limit today. Two are limited, per workspace and per caller\n(a person or an API key), because each call spends AI credits:\n\n| Endpoint                                                       | Limit                |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `POST /api/v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/ai/content-generations` | 10 requests a minute |\n| `POST /api/v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/ai/content-drafts`      | 30 requests a minute |\n\nSign-in and sign-up under `/api/auth` are limited too. Past a limit the API answers\n`429 Too Many Requests` with a `Retry-After` header. Limits per key may be added to other\nendpoints later, answered the same way. Handle `429` now (the SDKs do), and batch your work: list\nwith large pages, and use the bulk endpoints such as\n`POST …/channel-connections/{connectionId}/products/add`.',
